#X obj 561 237 symbol;
#X text 35 46 A formant is a prominent spectral peak produced by a resonance in a sound-producing system. Hence \, they reinforce spectral peaks at given frequencies with an amplitude boost. Most notably \, the shape of the mouth and vocal tract can produce multiple formants depending on the vowel \, but musical instruments also have formants \, like the body of a violin \, the tube of a clarinet or the soundboard of a piano \, which all introduce resonances that shape their timbre., f 52;
#X text 35 275 There are different Formant Synthesis techniques. A common and simple one is to feed an excitation signal \, such as a pulse train or noise \, through resonant filters tuned to the desired formant frequencies. Let's start with that., f 52;
